   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th adrenal cortical carcinoma & multiparameter scoring",
    "intro": "Apply the appropriate diagnostic algorithm by subtype and age: Weiss / Modified Weiss / Helsinki / Reticulin for conventional adult ACC, Lin-Weiss-Bisceglia for oncocytic (> 90%), and Wieneke for paediatric neoplasms. Report mitotic count per 10 mm2 (50 HPF) and Ki-67 labelling index.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Scoring systems & grading thresholds",
      "points": [
       "Weiss system (conventional adult): >= 3 of 9 criteria supports malignancy (high nuclear grade, > 5 mitoses/10 mm2, atypical mitoses, <= 25% clear cells, > 1/3 diffuse architecture, confluent necrosis, venous invasion, sinusoidal invasion, capsular invasion).",
       "Lin-Weiss-Bisceglia (oncocytic): any 1 major criterion (> 5 mitoses/10 mm2, atypical mitoses, or venous invasion) = carcinoma; minor criteria alone = uncertain malignant potential.",
       "Reticulin algorithm: disrupted reticulin framework plus any 1 of > 5 mitoses/10 mm2, tumour necrosis, or vascular invasion.",
       "Grade: Low-grade <= 20 mitoses/10 mm2 vs High-grade > 20 mitoses/10 mm2. Specify Ki-67 % (carcinomas typically > 5%; > 10–20% adverse). SF1 confirms adrenocortical lineage; IGF2 paranuclear granular staining in ~80%; nuclear beta-catenin and mutant p53 are adverse."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Adrenal Cortical Carcinoma",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ],
      "images": [
       {
